        {
          "line": 18,
          "text": "This finite-dimensional development uses the support-sensitive quantum relative entropy with natural logarithms. It proves the resolvent compression inequality for the negative logarithm and develops partial-trace and channel data processing through finite Stinespring dilation, using [[thm-it-quantum-relative-entropy-joint-convexity|joint convexity]] from Quantum Information Measures. The entropy consequences are strong subadditivity and nonnegativity of conditional mutual information; the measurement consequence is the [[thm-it-holevo-measurement-bound|finite Holevo bound]] established on that prerequisite page. States and positive semidefinite operators are both allowed where the stated relative entropy convention permits them. No infinite-dimensional extension or equality/recovery claim is made."
